## Sending files and images

If you need to upload any file as an attachment to a Slack message, just mention the full path of the file somewhere in the message and it will automatically be uploaded. Any of these work:

- "I'm attaching the image to this message: /Users/luo/work/luo-ji-pfp/luo_ji_pfp_v1.png"
- "I'm attaching the image to this message:\n\n/Users/luo/work/luo-ji-pfp/luo_ji_pfp_v1.png"
- "Attaching all 3 variations here ~/work/option1.jpg, ~/work/option2.jpg, ~/work/option3.jpg"

This isn't just limited to images — you can use this format to upload any file format supported on Slack. Tilde paths (`~/...`) are expanded automatically.

**NOTE:** If you want the team to open a file in the file browser instead (preferred for markdown, HTML, or images when they're on desktop), give a Tailscale file browser link instead of a bare path. Example:

- `<http://100.89.76.77:8888/browse/Users/luo/work/vision.md|Here's the vision doc>`

File browser links will NOT trigger an upload — only bare paths do.

